[13079]="7002E58D\n1\tBring the Tokens of Hytbold to Harsterre\030Gather Tokens of Hytbold (quantity: see journal)\tThere is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.\n",
[13080]="7002E597\n1\tBring the Tokens of Hytbold to Hargar\030Gather Tokens of Hytbold (quantity: see journal)\tThere is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.\n",
[13081]="7006715F\n1\tCollect the pivotal crate\tYared has asked you to pick up the pivotal crate and attempt to win The Stacking Game.\n2\tWin the Stacking Game by placing the pivotal crate at the winning spot\tMake your way to the top of Yared's stack of crates and set the pivotal crate there to win The Stacking Game.\n3\tTalk to Yared\tYared is waiting for you below.\n",
[13082]="70026E4C\n1\tFind the first piece of the ritual set\030Find the second piece of the ritual set\030Find the third piece of the ritual set\tThe items for the ritual feast can be found somewhere in Lhan Tarren. You should help Elder Riagán find the items that he has lost, for they will be needed tonight at the feast, and it seems as though his old mind has forgotten their whereabouts.\n2\tBring the pieces of the ritual set to Elder Riagán\tElder Riagán can be found in Lhan Tarren, musing over the whereabouts of the items you found. You should bring the pieces of the ritual set to Elder Riagán for tonight's feast.\n",
[13083]="7005F6BD\n1\tFind evidence of Old Skárhogg's presence at Skelstrand\tOld Skárhogg might be found stalking the waters around Skelstrand. Orti has asked you to find evidence of Old Skárhogg's presence at Skelstrand and put an end to the dangerous ukhrash before it can hinder the Gabil'akkâ in Gloomingtarn.\n2\tExamine the slain Angmarim\tOld Skárhogg might be found stalking the waters around Skelstrand. You have discovered an Angmarim slain by a massive ukhrash, likely Old Skárhogg. You should remain alert and defeat Old Skárhogg.\n3\tTalk to Orti\tOrti can be found at Watchers' Roost in Gloomingtarn. Although it seemingly posed an equally dire threat to the Iron Crown in Gloomingtarn, you have defeated Old Skárhogg and made the western banks of Durthuzâram safe once again. You should return to Orti.\n",
[13084]="70037E5C\n1\tFind the talking crow\tThe crow was last seen in the western portion of Aldburg. Bertred wants you to find his talking crow and attempt to speak with it in order to prove that he is not mad.\n2\tSpeak with the talking crow\tThe talking crow is in the western part of Aldburg. Bertred asked to to attempt to speak with the talking crow.\n3\tTalk to the meddling child\tThere is a child hiding behind the bush near the crow. You should speak with the child.\n4\tTalk to Bertred\030Talk to the meddling child\tBertred is at his home in Aldburg. The decision lies with you: speak with the child and let him go or speak with Bertred and bring the wrath of the mad Quartermaster down upon the child.\n",
[13085]="7004853B\n1\tUnlock the Standing Stone to receive your reward\tUnlock the Standing Stone to receive your reward.\n2\tUnlock the Standing Stone to receive your reward\tUnlock the Standing Stone to receive your reward.\n3\tUnlock the Standing Stone to receive your reward\tUnlock the Standing Stone to receive your reward.\n4\tUnlock the Standing Stone to receive your reward\tUnlock the Standing Stone to receive your reward.\n5\tUnlock the Standing Stone to receive your reward\tUnlock the Standing Stone to receive your reward.\n6\tReceive your reward from the Standing Stone\tReceive for reward from the Standing Stone\n",
[13086]="70062F49\n1\tCollect lichen (total: 8)\tHafren has asked you to collect lichen from standing stones. Standing stones can be found in Tyrn Gorthad.\n2\tReturn to Hafren\tYou should bring the lichen you collected to Hafren. Hafren is at Gerwyn's convoy, in northern Cardolan.\n",
[13087]="70003248\n1\tPresent the Elf-stone at the standing stone\030Defeat the Mound-wight Master\tThe white standing stone is in the old Edain mounds north-east of Glamír's home, near the ruins of an old building. Glamír told you to take the Elf-stone to the Edain mounds and place it upon the largest standing stone. He believes the creature whose will governs the wights of Haudh Lin may be drawn into the open by its presence.\n2\tBring the Elf-stone to Glamír\tGlamír is within the ruin, south-west of the ancient Edain mounds. As Glamír foretold, the Elf-stone drew forth the master of the wights. You should return to Glamír with news of your victory over the creature.\n",
[13088]="7006421A\n1\tDefeat Orcs at Uruk-gashan in the Dimrill Dale (total: 12)\030Collect planks of ilex wood (total: 8)\tOrcs and planks of ilex wood can be found at Uruk-gashan in the Dimrill Dale. Byrski Hardprow has asked you to fend off the Orcs lurking in the Dimrill Dale, and he has also asked you to collect planks of ilex wood.\n2\tDeliver the planks of ilex wood to Byrski Hardprow at Mekhem-bizru\tByrski Hardprow can be found at Mekhem-bizru in the Dimrill Dale. You have collected a number of planks of ilex wood and driven off many of the Orcs at Uruk-gashan. You should return to Byrski Hardprow.\n3\tHelp Byrski Hardprow build a ship\tYou should help Byrski Hardprow to build a ship for his expedition.\n4\tTalk to Byrski Hardprow\tByrski Hardprow can be found at Mekhem-bizru in the Dimrill Dale.\n5\tHelp Byrski to build a ship worthy of witnessing Durin's Crown\tYou should help Byrski Hardprow to build a ship for his expedition, but maybe try a bit harder this time.\n6\tTalk to Byrski Hardprow\tByrski Hardprow can be found at Mekhem-bizru in the Dimrill Dale. You have successfully built a suitable ship for your expedition onto the Mirrormere. You should talk to Byrski Hardprow.\n7\tTalk to Byrski Hardprow\tByrski Hardprow can be found at Mekhem-bizru in the Dimrill Dale.\n8\tTalk to Byrski Hardprow\tByrski Hardprow can be found at Mekhem-bizru in the Dimrill Dale. You have helped Byrski Hardprow to witness Durin's Crown in the Mirrormere. You should talk to Byrski Hardprow.\n",
})
